<Layout title="Terms & Conditions — CourseDepth" description="The rules that apply when you use CourseDepth and our Udemy course reviews.">
<Header />
<section class="page-hero"><div class="container"><h1>Terms & Conditions</h1><p>The rules that apply when you use CourseDepth and our Udemy course reviews.</p></div></section>
<section class="section"><div class="container" style="max-width:760px">
<h2>1. About these terms</h2>
<p>CourseDepth ("we") provides free comparison data, ratings and Udemy course reviews for informational purposes. By using this website you agree to these terms.</p>
<h2>2. Accuracy of information</h2>
<p>Course detailspoint — rating, price, duration and update dates — come from public provider feeds and are provided as-is. Prices and availability change often; always confirm the final price on the provider's checkout page.</p>
<h2>3. Reviews you submit</h2>
<p>Reviews you write must be your own honest experience. You keep ownership of your content, but you grant us a licence to display it on the site. We may remove reviews that are spam, abusive, promotional or off-topic.</p>
<h2>4. Affiliate links</h2>
<p>Some course links are affiliate links. If you buy through them we may earn a commission at no extra cost to you. Affiliates never influence ratings, ordering or whether a review is published.</p>
<h2>5. Limitation of liability</h2>
<p>To the maximum extent permitted by law, CourseDepth is not liable for decisions you make based on the site, including purchases made on third-party platforms such as Udemy.</p>
<h2>6. Changes</h2>
<p>We may update these terms at any time. The latest version is always published on this page. Last updated: October 2026.</p>
<p style="color:var(--muted);font-size:14px;margin-top:28px">Questions? <a href="/contact" style="font-weight:700">Contact us</a> — read more in our <a href="/about-us" style="font-weight:700">about page</a>.</p>
</div></section>
<Footer />
</Layout>
